    "lab-2026-11-21-incumbent-stack-two-machines": {
      "id": "5pmfwt8m7evb67e2ekyfebnxht",
      "created": "2026-11-21T03:06:31Z",
      "hash": "sha256:8d76018624e12c095c5466500979b02aab7b9ab806cf1e325a91e799c6479b33",
      "kind": "thread",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "slug": "lab-2026-11-21-stack-split-two-machines",
          "id": "7nx65h9vk6q4v05qrpy6ta1zw8",
          "version": 2,
          "html": "<div class=\"blyg-tk-gen\">\n<p><strong>Today&#39;s computing stack straddles two world machines</strong></p>\n<p>In <a href=\"https://worldmachines.org/theory\">World Machines</a> theory, Modernity, which pulls history toward one destination, is in its declining Dusk, and Divergence, where outcomes depend on local conditions, is in its Day. On our reading, digital computing&#39;s chips-and-scaling layer looks like late Modernity: frontier training costs up 2.4× a year, a concentrated chip supply. But energy is only 2–6% of that cost, and ordinary market economics explains the concentration just as well. The idea that AI&#39;s deployment belongs to Divergence has no support yet.</p>\n<p>How sure: an untested idea, weakened by adversarial review. <a href=\"https://github.com/msmsim/kinocomputing-lab/blob/main/analyses/a001-incumbent-stack-in-the-machines/ANALYSIS.md\">The working analysis</a>.</p>\n</div>"
        },
        {
          "slug": "lab-2026-11-21-physics-bodies-placement",
          "id": "1zqse6syhdhrn26zb7b0thb5sx",
          "version": 2,
          "html": "<div class=\"blyg-tk-gen\">\n<p><strong>Physics computing as repair, body computing as new ground</strong></p>\n<p>Two families of <a href=\"https://www.kinocomputing.com/alternative-paradigms\">alternative computing</a> sit differently in <a href=\"https://worldmachines.org/theory\">World Machines</a> theory, on our reading. &quot;Let physics compute&quot; (analog, photonic, thermodynamic chips) is mostly pitched as doing the digital computer&#39;s job more cheaply: a repair for Modernity in its declining Dusk, judged by the old machine&#39;s yardstick. &quot;Let bodies compute&quot; (living tissue, organoids, embodied systems) reads closer to Divergence, where results are local by nature.</p>\n<p>How sure: an untested idea, weakened by adversarial review. The bodies half is partly true by definition, and the yardstick half rests on thin evidence. <a href=\"https://github.com/msmsim/kinocomputing-lab/blob/main/analyses/a001-incumbent-stack-in-the-machines/ANALYSIS.md\">The working analysis</a>.</p>\n</div>"
        }
      ],
