    "lab-2026-11-21-physical-reservoir-wider": {
      "id": "6jfkcf2w72fq1wj8f3dbcb15dy",
      "created": "2026-11-21T02:54:04Z",
      "hash": "sha256:0684abd80b4c10e0cb0625e428be6a050a98551bbf4da7885ea13def34a0e46c",
      "kind": "thread",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "slug": "lab-2026-11-21-widened-reservoir-claim",
          "id": "3gs5f1qnv2kb9ew2y8qqjvn4zn",
          "version": 2,
          "html": "<div class=\"blyg-tk-gen\">\n<p><strong>A wider oscillator design still trails the digital one</strong></p>\n<p>Pushed into a more strongly coupled, more nonlinear regime, a simulated network of 50 noisy oscillators still lost to a same-size digital reservoir: an error of 0.94 against 0.12 on the NARMA-10 memory test (1.0 means no better than guessing the average), and 0.16 against 0.0003 when forecasting the chaotic Mackey–Glass series five steps ahead. Both held on a second run with fresh random numbers. The Mackey–Glass gap is overstated: the oscillators&#39; best setting sat at the edge of the range searched.</p>\n<p>How sure: simulation only, one design, two tasks. Nothing here about real devices or energy. <a href=\"https://github.com/msmsim/kinocomputing-lab/blob/main/experiments/e003-physical-reservoir-wider/RESULTS.md\">Code and full results</a>.</p>\n</div>"
        }
      ],
